# Enforced as of 2026-08-24: this repo was made public (decision made and
# approved by the repo owner) specifically to unlock GitHub's "Require
# review from Code Owners" branch protection setting, which 403's on a
# private repo without GitHub Pro. Branch protection on `main` now requires
# a code-owner review from this file plus the required CI jobs green before
# any merge, `enforce_admins: true` (no bypass, including for the owner).
#
# @SageCarter98 is currently the only collaborator on this repo, so the
# required-approval count is configured as 1, not EC-202's literal "two
# approvers, one Engineering Lead" — GitHub's review-count setting is
# per-branch, not conditional on which path changed, so it can't require
# 2 only for these zones. Revisit once a second engineer joins.
#
# EC-501 closed 2026-08-26: ci.yml's protected-test-integrity job now fails
# a PR if an existing test case in any of the three files below was changed
# or deleted (a content hash, not just title, so a kept title with a
# gutted body still fails). Review of these files is still required
# regardless — this catches what a distracted reviewer misses, it doesn't
# replace the reviewer. One real gap remains: branch protection's
# required-status-checks list is a GitHub repo setting, not something this
# repo's files can express, and this Agent is barred from touching branch
# protection rules (EC-201) same as CI config itself — a human still needs
# to add "protected-test-integrity" to that list by hand for a red result
# here to actually block a merge, not just show as a failing check.

